Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.20,0:00:02.69,Default,,0,0,0,,In November 2025,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.69,0:00:06.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Microsoft's CEO said something strange.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.57,0:00:09.17,Default,,0,0,0,,His company may have a bunch of AI chips
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.17,0:00:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,sitting in inventory – that it can't plug in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.54,0:00:14.26,Default,,0,0,0,,The chips weren't the problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.26,0:00:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The problem, in his words, was power.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.83,0:00:18.40,Default,,0,0,0,,So here's the question:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.40,0:00:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,will electricity become the ceiling on AI?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.77,0:00:24.93,Default,,0,0,0,,My answer is yes. But not in the way you think.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.33,0:00:27.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Because the thing that's really running
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.56,0:00:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,out might not be electricity at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.62,0:00:32.60,Default,,0,0,0,,First, why does AI need so much
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.60,0:00:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,electricity in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.04,0:00:37.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Data centers are built from racks,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.24,0:00:39.77,Default,,0,0,0,,tall cabinets packed with computers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.02,0:00:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,In 2024, the average rack drew under 8 kilowatts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.55,0:00:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,A single rack of Nvidia's GB200 AI
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.12,0:00:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,system is estimated to draw around 120.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.67,0:00:56.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That's roughly fifteen times as much, in one cabinet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.45,0:00:59.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Now fill a whole campus with them. Elon Musk's xAI
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.98,0:01:03.52,Default,,0,0,0,,already runs about one and a half gigawatts of its
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.52,0:01:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,own power plants for its data centers in Memphis.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.44,0:01:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,One gigawatt, running around the clock,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.48,0:01:14.51,Default,,0,0,0,,is about what 800,000 average American homes use.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.76,0:01:19.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Add it all up, and in 2024, data centers worldwide
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.21,0:01:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,used about 415 terawatt-hours of electricity.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.67,0:01:25.82,Default,,0,0,0,,That's around one and a half percent
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.82,0:01:28.29,Default,,0,0,0,,of all the electricity the world uses.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.89,0:01:31.87,Default,,0,0,0,,One and a half percent doesn't sound like a crisis.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.12,0:01:36.87,Default,,0,0,0,,But the International Energy Agency expects it to more
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.87,0:01:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,than double by 2030, to around 945 terawatt-hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.72,0:01:44.89,Default,,0,0,0,,That's slightly more than all of Japan uses today.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.14,0:01:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,And it's concentrated. The United States alone accounts
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.27,0:01:53.07,Default,,0,0,0,,for about 45 percent of data center electricity.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.32,0:01:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Through 2030, data centers are expected to drive
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.71,0:02:00.72,Default,,0,0,0,,nearly half of America's growth in electricity demand.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.52,0:02:03.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You might think: chips keep getting
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.35,0:02:05.43,Default,,0,0,0,,more efficient. Won't that solve it?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.68,0:02:08.01,Default,,0,0,0,,They are getting more efficient.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.01,0:02:11.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Nvidia says its newest system delivers up to 25
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.44,0:02:14.73,Default,,0,0,0,,times more performance at the same power than
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.73,0:02:18.22,Default,,0,0,0,,the previous generation, on certain AI tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.47,0:02:21.57,Default,,0,0,0,,And yet, data center electricity use has
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.57,0:02:24.74,Default,,0,0,0,,grown about 12 percent a year since 2017,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.74,0:02:29.36,Default,,0,0,0,,more than four times faster than electricity use overall.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.61,0:02:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,This is an old story. In 1865, the economist William
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.56,0:02:37.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Stanley Jevons noticed that more efficient steam engines
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.81,0:02:41.73,Default,,0,0,0,,didn't cut Britain's coal use. They increased it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.98,0:02:44.15,Default,,0,0,0,,When something gets cheaper to use,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.15,0:02:46.33,Default,,0,0,0,,we find far more ways to use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.58,0:02:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheaper AI means more AI. Efficiency doesn't
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.80,0:02:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,shrink the bill. It grows the appetite.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.66,0:02:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's what most people miss.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.00,0:02:58.52,Default,,0,0,0,,The world isn't running out of electricity.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.52,0:03:01.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It's running out of time to connect it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.26,0:03:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,A data center is just a building.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.50,0:03:06.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Feeding it takes a whole chain: power plants,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.55,0:03:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,transmission lines, transformers.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.23,0:03:12.19,Default,,0,0,0,,And every link in that chain has a waiting line.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.44,0:03:14.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Start with power plants. In the US,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.95,0:03:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,a new power project has to apply to
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.46,0:03:20.53,Default,,0,0,0,,connect to the grid, then wait its turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.78,0:03:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,At the end of 2025, more than 2,000 gigawatts of
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.46,0:03:28.56,Default,,0,0,0,,generation and storage were sitting in those lines.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.81,0:03:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,For projects that finally came online in 2025,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.23,0:03:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,the typical wait from application to
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.90,0:03:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,switching on was more than five years.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.17,0:03:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,And most never make it at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.49,0:03:44.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Of everything that applied between 2000 and 2020,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.27,0:03:46.86,Default,,0,0,0,,only 13 percent was ever built.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.11,0:03:49.34,Default,,0,0,0,,New transmission lines in advanced
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.34,0:03:52.43,Default,,0,0,0,,economies take four to eight years to build.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.68,0:03:55.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Large power transformers now have lead
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.39,0:03:58.38,Default,,0,0,0,,times of up to four years, and prices have
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.38,0:04:01.43,Default,,0,0,0,,jumped roughly 80 percent in five years.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.68,0:04:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Gas turbines? GE Vernova,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.88,0:04:07.66,Default,,0,0,0,,one of the biggest makers, said in December
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.66,0:04:11.29,Default,,0,0,0,,2025 that it was sold out through 2028.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.54,0:04:13.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The IEA estimates that, unless these
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.98,0:04:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,bottlenecks are fixed, around 20 percent of
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.90,0:04:20.23,Default,,0,0,0,,planned data center projects could be delayed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.48,0:04:23.88,Default,,0,0,0,,In September 2026, Morgan Stanley put a
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.88,0:04:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,number on the gap: a shortfall of about 32
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.54,0:04:31.48,Default,,0,0,0,,gigawatts for US data centers through 2028.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.73,0:04:34.05,Default,,0,0,0,,That's roughly a third of what they need.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.30,0:04:36.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Chips move on product cycles.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.35,0:04:39.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Power moves on permit and construction cycles,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.61,0:04:42.21,Default,,0,0,0,,and those run five years and more.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.01,0:04:45.81,Default,,0,0,0,,When something is scarce, its price tells you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.06,0:04:49.24,Default,,0,0,0,,PJM runs the power grid across all or
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.24,0:04:53.06,Default,,0,0,0,,parts of 13 US states and Washington, D.C.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.31,0:04:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Every year, it holds an auction
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.25,0:04:56.95,Default,,0,0,0,,for future power supply.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.20,0:05:00.27,Default,,0,0,0,,For 2024 to 2025, the price was
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.27,0:05:03.85,Default,,0,0,0,,about 29 dollars per megawatt-day.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.10,0:05:08.11,Default,,0,0,0,,For 2027 to 2028, it hit 333 dollars,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.11,0:05:11.57,Default,,0,0,0,,the maximum the rules allowed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.82,0:05:14.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Analysts estimate that without the cap,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.58,0:05:17.05,Default,,0,0,0,,it would have been close to 530.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.30,0:05:19.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And even at that price, the auction still
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.82,0:05:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,fell short of its reliability target.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.54,0:05:28.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The reason? PJM's demand forecast jumped by 5,250 megawatts,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.43,0:05:32.56,Default,,0,0,0,,almost entirely because of data centers.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.81,0:05:35.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And that cost doesn't stay with tech companies.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.70,0:05:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,In Washington, D.C., one utility's
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.55,0:05:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,residential customers saw bills rise about
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.06,0:05:45.50,Default,,0,0,0,,21 dollars a month starting in June 2025,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.50,0:05:49.29,Default,,0,0,0,,around 10 of it from these capacity prices.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.09,0:05:52.06,Default,,0,0,0,,So the tech giants stopped waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.31,0:05:56.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Microsoft signed a deal to bring back a reactor
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.20,0:06:00.02,Default,,0,0,0,,at Three Mile Island, which shut down in 2019.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.02,0:06:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It's now expected back online in 2027.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.62,0:06:07.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Google signed up for small nuclear reactors from a
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.69,0:06:11.69,Default,,0,0,0,,company called Kairos Power: up to 500 megawatts,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.69,0:06:16.30,Default,,0,0,0,,with the first targeted for 2030 and the rest by 2035.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.55,0:06:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Notice the dates. Even the fixes run
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.79,0:06:21.24,Default,,0,0,0,,on the grid's clock, not the chip's.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.49,0:06:23.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Others are skipping the grid entirely.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.00,0:06:27.70,Default,,0,0,0,,One analysis counted 59 US data center projects
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.70,0:06:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,planning about 90 gigawatts of their own on-site power.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.48,0:06:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,That's more than a quarter of all planned
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.84,0:06:37.12,Default,,0,0,0,,data center capacity in the country.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.37,0:06:40.10,Default,,0,0,0,,And 92 percent of those projects were
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.10,0:06:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,announced since the start of 2025.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.20,0:06:46.08,Default,,0,0,0,,But here's the catch. As of mid-2026,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.08,0:06:48.72,Default,,0,0,0,,only about 2 gigawatts of that was
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.72,0:06:51.72,Default,,0,0,0,,actually running. Roughly 2 percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.97,0:06:54.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Announcing a power plant is easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.06,0:06:56.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Building one is the bottleneck.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.49,0:07:00.04,Default,,0,0,0,,It got strange. In December 2025, Crusoe,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.04,0:07:03.34,Default,,0,0,0,,a company that builds AI data centers,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.34,0:07:07.25,Default,,0,0,0,,ordered 29 gas turbines from Boom Supersonic,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.25,0:07:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,a startup best known for designing supersonic jets.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.13,0:07:13.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, in September 2026,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.99,0:07:17.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Crusoe walked away from that deal and turned
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.42,0:07:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,to established suppliers like GE Vernova.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.06,0:07:23.02,Default,,0,0,0,,When time is the bottleneck,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.02,0:07:26.37,Default,,0,0,0,,an untested machine is a risk few can afford.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.17,0:07:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Now flip the map.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.71,0:07:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,China generates more than twice as
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.11,0:07:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,much electricity as the United States.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.23,0:07:37.63,Default,,0,0,0,,In 2025 alone, it added more than 430
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.63,0:07:41.23,Default,,0,0,0,,gigawatts of wind and solar capacity.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.48,0:07:44.51,Default,,0,0,0,,BloombergNEF expects China to add more
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.51,0:07:47.85,Default,,0,0,0,,than six times as much generation capacity
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.85,0:07:50.84,Default,,0,0,0,,as the US over the next five years.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.09,0:07:54.24,Default,,0,0,0,,One business school researcher put it simply:
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.24,0:07:57.26,Default,,0,0,0,,the US has the chips and is short on power.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.26,0:08:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,China has the power and is short on chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.66,0:08:02.73,Default,,0,0,0,,So electricity isn't one ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.73,0:08:06.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a different ceiling, depending on where you stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.17,0:08:08.62,Default,,0,0,0,,So here's my call.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.87,0:08:10.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Electricity won't stop AI.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.64,0:08:14.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Too much money is chasing this problem for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.37,0:08:16.96,Default,,0,0,0,,But for the next few years, power will
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.96,0:08:19.62,Default,,0,0,0,,decide three things: how fast AI grows,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.62,0:08:22.13,Default,,0,0,0,,where it gets built, and who wins.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.38,0:08:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,The winners won't just be the ones with the best models.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.54,0:08:28.33,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll be the ones who locked in power early.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.58,0:08:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd go further: by the end of this decade,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.08,0:08:33.53,Default,,0,0,0,,a guaranteed grid connection may be worth
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.53,0:08:35.94,Default,,0,0,0,,more than the chips you plug into it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.34,0:08:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,And if I'm wrong, it'll be because the grid
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.28,0:08:42.63,Default,,0,0,0,,suddenly started moving at chip speed: new lines,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.63,0:08:46.33,Default,,0,0,0,,plants and transformers arriving in two or three years
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.33,0:08:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,instead of five or more. That's the signal to watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.89,0:08:52.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What does this mean for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.73,0:08:55.49,Default,,0,0,0,,If you live where data centers are booming,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.49,0:08:59.42,Default,,0,0,0,,part of AI's bill may already be on your electricity bill.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.67,0:09:03.18,Default,,0,0,0,,And next time someone says AI is limited by chips,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.18,0:09:05.23,Default,,0,0,0,,remember Microsoft's problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.23,0:09:08.17,Default,,0,0,0,,The chips were there. The power wasn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.42,0:09:11.14,Default,,0,0,0,,So which do you think runs out first: chips,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.14,0:09:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,or electricity? Tell me in the comments.
